+      # The blackbox exporter fetches Keycloak's discovery document for the
+      # homelab realm at each scrape, once a minute. On 2026-09-25 it answered
+      # 502 for the whole outage, which took down DHCPApp and four other apps. probe_success is 0 when the exporter ran
+      # the probe and it failed; when the exporter is down or its scrape fails
+      # there is no probe_success at all, which OIDCDiscoveryUnprobed takes, so
+      # neither reads as a passing probe. In 42 days of history keycloak-prd had
+      # no available replica for at most 3 m outside the outage, which reads as
+      # a failing probe for at most 4 m; 5 m passes that.
+      # tests/alert-rules/oidc-discovery.yml walks these edges on synthetic series.
+      - name: oidc-discovery
+        rules:
+          - alert: OIDCDiscoveryFailing
+            expr: |
+              probe_success{job="oidc-discovery"} == 0
+            for: 5m
+            labels:
+              severity: critical
+            annotations:
+              summary: 'OIDC discovery at auth.ginbov.nl has failed for 5m'
+              description: >-
+                {{ $labels.instance }} does not return the homelab realm's
+                discovery document, so apps that log in through Keycloak cannot
+                start, as DHCPApp could not on 2026-09-25. Check that
+                keycloak-prd's pods are Ready (an image pull stuck there was the
+                2026-09-25 cause), then the ingress in front of it. The probe's
+                own log is at
+                http://blackbox-exporter.prometheus-prd.svc:9115/ from inside
+                the cluster.
+          - alert: OIDCDiscoveryUnprobed
+            expr: |
+              absent(probe_success{job="oidc-discovery"})
+            for: 10m
+            labels:
+              severity: warning
+            annotations:
+              summary: 'OIDC discovery is unwatched: no probe result for 10m'
+              description: >-
+                Prometheus has had no result from the oidc-discovery probe for
+                10 m, so OIDCDiscoveryFailing cannot fire. The blackbox-exporter
+                pod in prometheus-prd is down or not Ready, or its scrape fails;
+                check the oidc-discovery target in Prometheus.
+
+      # srviac's dhcp-probe timer (Ansible role dhcp_probe) sends a relay-style
+      # DISCOVER to the DHCP Service every 3 m from outside the cluster and
+      # writes the result into node-exporter's textfile collector, which the
+      # homelab-nodes job scrapes. node-exporter serves the last result until
+      # the next one, and a probe run that errors writes nothing.
+      #
+      # DHCPNotAnswering resolves only on a probe that got an OFFER: while no
+      # probe result is scraped (srviac down or not scraped) it holds its own
+      # ALERTS state. A rollout or reboot drops the Service's announcement for
+      # up to 6 m (the loadbalancers group), which reads as no OFFER for up to
+      # 10 m 10 s at the probe's 3 m cadence and the 1 m scrape; 12 m passes
+      # that.
+      #
+      # DHCPProbeStale fires once the last probe run that finished is over
+      # 15 m old, which three missed runs in a row do not reach, or no result
+      # has been scraped for 15 m. It fires on prd until srviac's play has
+      # installed the probe.
+      # tests/alert-rules/dhcp.yml walks these edges on synthetic series.
+      - name: dhcp
+        rules:
+          - alert: DHCPNotAnswering
+            expr: |
+              max by (instance, server) (dhcp_probe_success{job="homelab-nodes"}) == 0
+              or
+              (
+                max by (instance, server) (ALERTS{alertname="DHCPNotAnswering"})
+                unless on () dhcp_probe_success{job="homelab-nodes"}
+              )
+            for: 12m
+            labels:
+              severity: critical
+            annotations:
+              summary: 'DHCP at {{ $labels.server }} has not answered a DISCOVER for 12m'
+              description: >-
+                srviac's relay-style DISCOVER to {{ $labels.server }} gets no
+                OFFER, so no client on the network gets a lease. On 2026-09-25
+                the dhcp pod in dnsmasq-prd was not Ready, so MetalLB did not
+                announce the Service: check LoadBalancerNotAnnounced and the
+                pod (kubectl -n dnsmasq-prd get pods). journalctl -u
+                dhcp-probe on srviac gives the probe's own view. This alert
+                resolves on the first probe that gets an OFFER.
+          - alert: DHCPProbeStale
+            expr: |
+              time() - max by (instance, server) (dhcp_probe_last_run_timestamp_seconds{job="homelab-nodes"}) > 15 * 60
+              or
+              absent_over_time(dhcp_probe_last_run_timestamp_seconds{job="homelab-nodes"}[15m])
+            labels:
+              severity: warning
+            annotations:
+              summary: 'DHCP is unwatched: no DHCP probe result from srviac for 15m'
+              description: >-
+                No dhcp-probe run on srviac has finished in the last 15 m, or
+                Prometheus has scraped none, so DHCPNotAnswering cannot tell
+                whether DHCP answers. srviac is down or its node-exporter is not
+                scraped (check the homelab-nodes target srviac.home:9100), or
+                the probe errors or its timer stopped (systemctl status
+                dhcp-probe.timer dhcp-probe.service on srviac).
+
 alertmanager:
   # See https://github.com/prometheus-community/helm-charts/blob/main/charts/alertmanager/values.yaml
   service:
